{
    "background_story": "Phoenix was a brilliant and fearless welder who had a passion for working with fire. Growing up in a family of artists, she was drawn to the creative possibilities of shaping metal with acetylene torches. After completing her apprenticeship, Phoenix started her own business, specializing in intricate sculptures and custom motorcycle parts. Her workshop was a haven of sparks and flames, where she would lose herself for hours, shaping and molding metal into breathtaking works of art. Phoenix's use of acetylene allowed her to achieve unparalleled precision and detail, earning her a reputation as one of the most innovative metalworkers in the city. Her art pieces were highly sought after, and she became known for her ability to transform raw metal into fiery, ethereal creations that seemed to come alive in the light.",
